sn22.81:5.11 | S: and that ignorance are also impermanent, conditioned, and dependently originated. | T: that ignorance is impermanent, conditioned, dependently arisen.
sn22.81:5.12 | S: That’s how you should know and see in order to end the defilements without delay. | T: When one knows and sees thus, bhikkhus, the immediate destruction of the taints occurs.
