## sn35.69
sn35.69:1.1 | S: At one time the venerables Sāriputta and Upasena were staying near Rājagaha in the Cool Grove, under the Cobra’s Hood Grotto. | T: On one occasion the Venerable Sāriputta and the Venerable Upasena were dwelling at Rajagaha in the Cool Grove, in the Snake’s Hood Grotto.
sn35.69:1.2 | S: Now at that time a viper fell on Upasena’s body. | T: Now on that occasion a viper had fallen on the Venerable Upasena’s body.
sn35.69:1.3 | S: He addressed the mendicants, | T: Then the Venerable Upasena addressed the bhikkhus thus:
sn35.69:1.4 | S: “Come, reverends, lift this body onto a cot and carry it outside | T: “Come, friends, lift this body of mine on to the bed and carry it outside before it is scattered right here like a handful of chaff.”
