## an8.6
an8.6:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, the eight worldly conditions revolve around the world, and the world revolves around the eight worldly conditions. | T: “Bhikkhus, these eight worldly conditions revolve around the world, and the world revolves around these eight worldly conditions.
an8.6:1.2 | S: What eight? | T: What eight?
an8.6:1.3 | S: Gain and loss, fame and disgrace, blame and praise, pleasure and pain. | T: Gain and loss, disrepute and fame, blame and praise, and pleasure and pain.
an8.6:1.4 | S: These eight worldly conditions revolve around the world, and the world revolves around these eight worldly conditions. | T: These eight worldly conditions revolve around the world, and the world revolves around these eight worldly conditions.
an8.6:2.1 | S: An unlearned ordinary person encounters gain and loss, fame and disgrace, blame and praise, and pleasure and pain. | T: “Bhikkhus, an uninstructed worldling meets gain and loss, disrepute and fame, blame and praise, and pleasure and pain.
